  "body": "**Link to problem area**: https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/client-server-api/#listing-rooms\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\nMy current understanding:\r\n1. the room directory shows a list of rooms deemed to be public\r\n2. rooms can be included or excluded from this list via `PUT /_matrix/client/v3/directory/list/room/{roomId}`\r\n3. I think(?) there is some relationship between join rules and this list. But the details aren't specified?\r\n  - Are rooms with join_rules `public` included in this list, unless they've been opted out?\r\n  - What about `knock` and `knock_restricted`?\r\n  - Can you try to mark an `invite-only` room as public?\r\n  - Does the homeserver have some discretion here?\r\n\r\nIn a nutshell, I'd like to see a short bit of prose which explains that the join rules and visibility are separate (but not orthogonal?) concepts.",
